- op: discuss  # b8d9
  at: '2026-04-15T16:44:46Z'  # b8d9
  by: agent  # b8d9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b8d9
  clock: 6  # b8d9
  nonce: b8d9  # b8d9
  message: "Verified on docspell — you were right. http4s is imported on hundreds of lines (org.http4s._, org.http4s.HttpRoutes, org.http4s.dsl.Http4sDsl, HttpRoutes.of[F], Http4sClientDsl, BlazeServerBuilder, etc.); build.sbt pulls http4sClient/http4sCirce/http4sDsl — yet `hypergumbo run` on ~/ALL_REPOS/repos_Apr12_2026/docspell produces profile.frameworks=[], profile.dev_frameworks=[], metrics.detected_frameworks=[]. `hypergumbo routes` on the same repo reports \"No API routes found\". So the YAML is present in the repo but the detector path never matches.\n\nLikely cause: http4s.yaml patterns match on `usage.kind=^call$, usage.name=^HttpRoutes$` but either (a) the Scala analyzer emits these as imports/instantiates rather than call, or (b) the emitted name is qualified (org.http4s.HttpRoutes) so the `^HttpRoutes$` regex misses. Also possible the framework-detection pass does not currently run on Scala symbols at all.\n\nPlay (lila) and Flask-AppBuilder (superset) are not cloned locally. Will verify whether the same YAML-present-but-detector-silent pattern applies once I have those repos — if yes, a single analyzer/pattern-format fix likely handles all three, and the superficial \"YAMLs exist\" claim was misleading.\n\nFiling a follow-up work item so this does not get lost behind the original ticket that was closed against WIP-PR-only evidence."  # b8d9
